  "title": "Everyone Can Tell Your Emails Were Written By AI",
  "description": "There is a free file on GitHub with 30,183 stars that names all 33 signs of AI writing and strips them out of anything you paste in. It is built on Wikipedia's own \"Signs of AI writing\" guide, the one their editors wrote to clean AI text out of the encyclopedia.\n\nIt runs two passes: it rewrites your text, then asks itself what still sounds AI generated and rewrites again. Same length, same points, none of the tells. Install it with one line, or use the prompt version with nothing to install.\n\nGet the full list of 33 tells with a before and after for each one here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1i_zRfIt2pZUqc9R4xnrPNEM3yyPrCHGvbNcC5wUb_Ik/edit?usp=sharing\n\n#Shorts #AIWriting #ClaudeAI",
  "publishedAt": "2026-07-29T11:33:40Z",
  "channel_name": "Sebastian Hardy | AI Marketing",
  "transcript": "There is a free file on GitHub with 30,183 stars that names all 33 signs of AI writing and strips them out of anything you paste in. It is built on Wikipedia's own \"Signs of AI writing\" guide, the one their editors wrote to clean AI text out of the encyclopedia.\n\nIt runs two passes: it rewrites your text, then asks itself what still sounds AI generated and rewrites again. Same length, same points, none of the tells. Install it with one line, or use the prompt version with nothing to install.\n\nGet the full list of 33 tells with a before and after for each one here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1i_zRfIt2pZUqc9R4xnrPNEM3yyPrCHGvbNcC5wUb_Ik/edit?usp=sharing\n\n#Shorts #AIWriting #ClaudeAI",
